<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
            http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!--
      Recover the window start for the REST of the old sittings (PRD 5.16.2).

      0430 restored only the rows where the start was not a guess at all: credited time equal to
      the head position means the sitting ran straight through from zero. The rest were left NULL
      because "head minus credited" is exact only when nothing was rewound.

      Owner's call: recover them too. The remaining rows are the ones that continued an episode
      from the middle, and for them the difference is the best statement we have about which
      stretch was heard - the alternative is not a better number, it is no retelling at all.

      The approximation is also bounded, and in the useful direction. A forward skip (ads) makes
      credited time SMALLER than the distance covered, so the computed start lands late and we
      under-claim - we simply retell less than was heard. A rewind makes credited time larger, so
      the start lands early; but a rewind means that stretch was heard twice, so the window still
      covers audio the owner actually listened to.

      Checked against the local shelf before writing this: of the three rows it touches, two are
      corroborated exactly - the preceding sitting of the same episode ends at the very
      millisecond this one is computed to start (Lex #500: 45:00, Hidden Brain: 45:00).

      GREATEST(0, ...) guards the rewind case from going negative; new rows are unaffected, the
      poller records their start first-hand.
    -->
    <changeSet id="0440-podcast-window-backfill-rest" author="danchuo">
        <sql>
            UPDATE podcast_session
            SET start_progress_ms = GREATEST(0, last_progress_ms - listened_ms)
            WHERE start_progress_ms IS NULL
              AND listened_ms > 0
        </sql>
    </changeSet>
</databaseChangeLog>
